This project page presents our survey on deep learning approaches for medical image-to-mesh reconstruction.
The paper reviews how to convert CT/MR images into simulation-ready 3D meshes for computational medicine and in-silico trials.
We organize existing methods into four technical families and summarize their strengths, limitations, and practical use cases.

To keep this page consistent with the portfolio style, the original grid-based layout is preserved.
Suggested figure slots below can be replaced with final paper figures (pipeline overview, method taxonomy, benchmark summary).

