Key contributions of this survey include: (1) a systematic categorization into template, statistical, generative, and implicit model families; (2) structured comparison across cardiac, neurovascular, and other anatomical scenarios; (3) a consolidated review of public datasets, loss functions, and evaluation metrics; and (4) analysis of open challenges such as topological correctness, geometric fidelity, and multimodal integration.

The review also highlights why image-to-mesh reconstruction is central to personalized medicine: simulation-ready meshes enable downstream tasks such as hemodynamic simulation, virtual device testing, and virtual population generation for safer and more efficient in-silico studies.

